A||||7||theogre||DIS Ignition News Flash!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡
Z||000000||theogre||07-11-99||05:41 PM||||NEWS NEWS NEWS!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡<p>MSD,  <A HREF="http://www.msdignition.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.msdignition.com/</A> , now makes a ignition controllers for DIS distributorless ignition motors. As many of you know DIS solid state ignition started in 1987 for the GM/Pontiac 4 cyl motor. Untill now there have been effectivly Zero aftermarket performance items for these motors which also changed the ECM and TBI unit. I have Email pending with MSD and will report again as soon as I know something. As posted it looks like the MSD DIS-2 system should fit, but the email askes exactly how.... I don't know about you, but I Hate cutting factory wire for any reason.
Z||000001||Patrick||07-14-99||04:47 PM||||<br>Well, that news flash really set this forum on fire! :)<p>I went to that site Ogre, and I was disappointed that there didn't appear to be anything mentioned about the ability to retard the ignition timing at an <b>idle</b>. <p>On the ‘87 2.5L, the timing at an idle as set by the ECM is supposed to be 38 degrees BTDC. This seems unbelievable to me, but I've heard this from several reliable sources. This would explain the relatively rough, uneven idle, and the high emissions at an idle. The only reason this engine ever passes a smog test is because the "cat" has to work furiously to burn up all the raw fuel leaving the engine. I was able to see the proof of this myself when I had my Fiero smog tested immediately before and after a new cat was installed with NO other modifications done to the engine. The difference in emission levels was amazing. My 2.5L happens to run very strong, so I don't believe that there is any other problem contributing to the rough idle and emission levels.<p>I would LOVE to be able to retard the ignition timing at an idle and then let the ECM take over at say 1500 RPM. Ogre, do you or anyone else have any comments on this?<p><br>
Z||000002||Cooter||07-14-99||09:01 PM||||Next time I get out my "dial back to zero" timing light I will throw it on the Iron Duke to see what is up at at idle. My timing is probably a little high because it spark knocks even with premium unleaded at light throttle. I will let y'all know how it goes.
Z||000003||mwbackus||07-14-99||11:08 PM||||Not really big news in the fiero channels, MSD has offered this for at least a year now.  You can currently get the MSD DIS-2 for the 2.5l from JEGS (part #121-6211) for $319.99.  Now if you all are really that set on a 4 cyl that has some REAL power, I know were you can get a fresh 300hp Super Duty for about $11,500. :-)
Z||000004||lowCG||07-14-99||11:41 PM||||Always wondered how my old 4cyl car could run so good! Never had a problem with emissions,used some alcohol,high temp thermostat;never had a problem with soldering and heat shrink tubing either.
Z||000005||theogre||07-15-99||06:51 PM||||Acording to the web site the product is pretty new... it wasn't there when a looked a few months ago.<p>Here is the respoce from MSD..... <p>&gt; 	Dear Sir,<br>&gt; <br>&gt; 	The MSD unit that we offer for the distributorless application is<br>&gt; the PN 6211, Dis-2 for 4 cylinder application.   This is the only product<br>&gt; that we offer for the distributorless ignitions.  You can hard wire the<br>&gt; unit if you do have access to the primary wires.  We do not offer coils<br>&gt; for these applications, possibly in the future. We are also releasing part<br>&gt; number 8870 which is the installation blocks for the GM distributorless<br>&gt; applications.  These are still being worked on and are not in production<br>&gt; right now.  They will hopefully be available by the end of summer.   Once<br>&gt; installed it will give you better gas mileage, performance, throttle<br>&gt; response, starting and over all driveability by increasing fuel burn with<br>&gt; the additional spark energy produced.  The amount of gains will very from<br>&gt; application to application but you will see a gain.<br>&gt; <br>&gt; 	Thanks,<br>&gt; 	MSD Tech<br>&gt; <br>&gt; <br>
Z||000006||mwbackus||07-16-99||11:14 AM||||Web sites that are not updated frequently...not too rare.. hehe.  Actually, I have literature that I obtained from MSD in 98 that shows the DIS-2 as a "New for 98" product that was "available now".  I do agree that the wireing harness/block has been unavailable up till now, but I dont make statements like that unless I can back them up. :-)
